      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab8"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-indirect-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 28, "y": 726,
      "width": 244, "height": 288,
      "text": "INDIRECT — Pre-Hepatic\n\nHF-ICU causes:\n• Mechanical hemolysis\n  (LVAD, ECMO, prosthetic\n  valves)\n• DIC / MAHA\n• Hematoma resorption\n• Gilbert syndrome\n  (TBili rarely >6; no\n  hepatocyte dysfunction)\n• Drug effects (atazanavir)\n\nWorkup:\n• CBC + differential\n• Peripheral smear\n• Reticulocyte count\n• LDH, haptoglobin\n• Direct Coombs (DAT)\n• Review LVAD/ECMO\n  hemolysis parameters\n• LDH:haptoglobin ratio",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab9"
    },

    {
      "id": "s1-direct-path",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 310, "y": 720,
      "width": 310, "height": 300,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#c92a2a", "backgroundColor": "#fff0f0",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab10"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-direct-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 318, "y": 726,
      "width": 294, "height": 288,
      "text": "DIRECT — Hepatic Causes\n\nStep 2: R Ratio\n(ALT÷ULN) ÷ (ALP÷ULN)\n  R>5 = Hepatocellular\n  R 2-5 = Mixed\n  R<2 = Cholestatic\n\nStep 3: RUQ Ultrasound\n→ Biliary dilation?\n  YES → Extrahepatic obstruction\n    (stones, malignancy, stricture)\n    → MRCP or ERCP\n  NO → Intrahepatic cause\n    → Hemodynamic assessment\n       (congestion vs hypoperfusion)\n    → Medication review (DILI)\n    → Sepsis-assoc. cholestasis\n    → TPN >2 wks",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab11"
    },

    {
      "id": "s1-hemo-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 40, "y": 1042,
      "width": 580, "height": 140,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#0c8599", "backgroundColor": "#e3fafc",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab12"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-hemo-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50, "y": 1050,
      "width": 560, "height": 125,
      "text": "HEMODYNAMIC PHENOTYPING (Echo ± PA Catheter)\n\nCongestion (↑ RAP, dilated IVC, severe TR):\n  → PVPI > 0.5: 81% Sn, 87% Sp for TBili elevation from congestion\n  → Rx: Aggressive diuresis; ultrafiltration if diuretic-resistant\n\nHypoperfusion (CI <2.2, cardiogenic shock) — \"Two-Hit\" required:\n  → ALT:LDH <1.5 favors ischemic hepatitis (ACLI) over viral\n  → Transaminases peak days 1–3; normalize 5–10 days if hemo improves\n  → Rx: Inotropes, MCS escalation (Impella, VA-ECMO, IABP)",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab13"
    },

    {
      "id": "s1-prog-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 40, "y": 1200,
      "width": 580, "height": 70,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#e67700", "backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab14"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-prog-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50, "y": 1208,
      "width": 560, "height": 56,
      "text": "PROGNOSIS: TBili = independent predictor of CV death + HF hospitalization (HFrEF)\nEven after adjustment for NT-proBNP. Also independent predictor of RV failure post-LVAD.\nSacubitril/valsartan reduced TBili 2.4% vs enalapril (PARADIGM-HF) [Suzuki 2020]",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ab15"
    },

