    },
    {
      "id": "sec6-hdr-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 690, "y": 1360,
      "width": 560, "height": 16,
      "text": "SECTION 6 — ALBUMIN",
      "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center", "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#ffffff", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ag1"
    },

    {
      "id": "s6-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 680, "y": 1400,
      "width": 580, "height": 400,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#0c8599", "backgroundColor": "#e3fafc",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ag2"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 690, "y": 1408,
      "width": 560, "height": 386,
      "text": "LOW ALBUMIN (Hypoalbuminemia) — present in ~32% of HF pts\n\nHalf-life ~20 days → reflects CHRONIC dysfunction\n(vs INR which reflects ACUTE synthetic failure)\n\nSTEP 1: Contributing mechanisms (often multifactorial)\n• Hepatic congestion → impaired synthesis\n• Systemic inflammation → cytokine-mediated suppression\n  of synthesis (primary driver — more than malnutrition)\n• Malnutrition / cardiac cachexia → inadequate substrate\n• Hemodilution → volume overload\n• Protein-losing enteropathy → gut edema from ↑ RAP\n• Nephrotic syndrome → urinary losses (check urine protein)\n\nSTEP 2: Workup\n• LFTs, INR (synthetic function panel)\n• Urine protein / urine albumin:creatinine ratio\n• CRP / ESR (inflammation)\n• Nutritional assessment (prealbumin, retinol-binding\n  protein if available)\n• Echo: IVC, RAP (hemodilution vs true hepatic impairment)\n\nSTEP 3: Management\n• Optimize decongestion (reduces hepatic congestion +\n  hemodilution)\n• Optimize oral nutrition (clearly improved outcomes in\n  malnourished HF patients)\n• IV albumin: controversial; routine use does not improve\n  outcomes. Consider selectively for refractory edema /\n  ascites + profound hypoalbuminemia on max diuretics\n\nELEVATED ALBUMIN: Almost always dehydration /\nhemoconcentration. Reassess volume status.\n\nPROGNOSIS: In-hospital mortality 4× higher with\nhypoalbuminemia in HF (OR 3.77). Predictive accuracy\ncomparable to BNP (pooled AUC 0.73). Independent\npredictor of outcomes post-LVAD. [El Iskandarani 2021]",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ag3"
    },

    {
