    },

    {
      "id": "s7-ac-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1200, "y": 1520,
      "width": 200, "height": 100,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#5c3bc2", "backgroundColor": "#ede7f6",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ah8"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7-ac-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1208, "y": 1526,
      "width": 184, "height": 88,
      "text": "Expected:\n• Warfarin → INR ↑\n• Anti-Xa DOACs may\n  falsely ↑ INR on\n  some assays\n→ Interpret in context\n  of therapeutic range",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ah9"
    },

    {
      "id": "s7-noac-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1920, "y": 1520,
      "width": 560, "height": 280,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#5c3bc2", "backgroundColor": "#ede7f6",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ah10"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7-noac-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1928, "y": 1526,
      "width": 544, "height": 268,
      "text": "STEP 2: Non-anticoagulated elevated INR\n(3 most common ICU causes):\n\n1. Vitamin K deficiency (39.6%):\n   ↓ FVII, FX, Protein C, Protein S\n   → Poor nutrition, antibiotics, biliary obstruction\n   → Rx: Vitamin K (IV or PO); plasma generally avoidable\n\n2. Liver disease pattern (35.4%):\n   ↓ FV, ↓/normal fibrinogen, ↑ FVIII\n   → Impaired hepatic synthetic function\n   → In HF: correlates with TBili, GGT, IVC diameter,\n     TR severity, neurohormonal activation\n   → Rx: Treat underlying cause (decongestion in HF)\n   → Plasma NOT appropriate for routine INR correction\n     in liver disease\n\n3. Occult DOAC effect (14.6%):\n   → Anti-Xa DOAC detected on assay despite no reported use\n\nACLI-specific: ~80–84% of ACLI patients show ≥50%\ndrop in prothrombin activity (unusual in viral hepatitis)\n→ helps distinguish cardiogenic from viral etiology\n\nPersistent coagulopathy despite hemo optimization\n→ suggests progression to cardiac cirrhosis",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ah11"
    },

    {
      "id": "s7-prog-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1320, "y": 1820,
      "width": 580, "height": 60,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#e67700", "backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ah12"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7-prog-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1328, "y": 1828,
      "width": 564, "height": 46,
      "text": "PROGNOSIS: INR is an independent predictor of all-cause mortality in ADHF\n(HR 1.89 per 0.1 increase) — higher prognostic value than MELD or MELD-XI\n[Okada 2016]. INR + TBili + Albumin = hepatic synthetic function triad.",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ah13"
    },

    {
      "id": "synth-hdr",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 400, "y": 1920,
      "width": 1600, "height": 36,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "#1864ab",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ai0"
    },
    {
      "id": "synth-hdr-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 410, "y": 1930,
      "width": 1580, "height": 16,
      "text": "SYNTHETIC FUNCTION PANEL — Apply to ALL Patterns",
      "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center", "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#ffffff", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ai1"
    },

    {
      "id": "synth-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 400, "y": 1960,
      "width": 1600, "height": 200,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#1864ab", "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ai2"
    },
    {
      "id": "synth-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 415, "y": 1968,
      "width": 1570, "height": 185,
      "text": "Albumin ↓ (t½ ~20 days) → chronic hepatic synthetic dysfunction / malnutrition / inflammation / hemodilution\nINR ↑ (t½ hours–days) → ACUTE hepatic synthetic failure; if INR >1.5 + encephalopathy → Acute Liver Failure (ALF) criteria → hepatology / transplant consult\nTBili + INR + Cr → calculate MELD-Na score (prognostic + transplant listing)\nAlbumin low + INR ↑ + ascites → calculate Child-Pugh score\nPlatelets ↓ + splenomegaly → portal hypertension / cardiac cirrhosis?\n\nINR interpretation by pattern in ACLI: ~80–84% of patients show ≥50% drop in prothrombin activity → distinguishes cardiogenic from viral hepatitis\nALF Criteria: INR >1.5 + hepatic encephalopathy in absence of pre-existing cirrhosis → emergent hepatology + transplant evaluation\n\nPre-LVAD / Pre-Transplant evaluation: Persistent hyperbilirubinemia + abnormal imaging → liver biopsy may be required. Noninvasive tools (including liver stiffness MRE) cannot reliably differentiate congestion from fibrosis in this population [Lemmer 2018]",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "ai3"
    },

    {
      "id": "summary-hdr",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 400, "y": 2200,
      "width": 1600, "height": 36,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "#343a40",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "aj0"
    },
    {
      "id": "summary-hdr-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 410, "y": 2210,
      "width": 1580, "height": 16,
      "text": "SUMMARY TABLE — Lab Parameters in the HF-ICU",
      "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center", "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#ffffff", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "aj1"
    },

    {
      "id": "summary-box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 400, "y": 2240,
      "width": 1600, "height": 240,
      "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#495057", "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "aj2"
    },
    {
      "id": "summary-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 412, "y": 2248,
      "width": 1576, "height": 225,
      "text": "Parameter     Most Common HF-ICU Cause (↑)            Key Low Value Note                  Prognostic Significance\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nTBili          Congestive hepatopathy (cholestatic)      Not typically relevant              Indep. predictor CV death + HF hosp\nALP            Congestive hepatopathy (↑ RAP / TR)       Acute illness, malnutrition, Zn     ↑ 180-day mortality in ADHF (SURVIVE)\nGGT            Congestive hepatopathy + alcohol          Not clinically significant          Inversely assoc. with survival in HF\nAST/ALT       ACLI >20×ULN (two-hit: cong + hypoperf)  B6 deficiency / sarcopenia         ↑ 31-day + 180-day mortality (SURVIVE)\nLDH            ACLI (ALT:LDH <1.5), hemolysis, ischemia  Rare genetic deficiency            GALACTIC-HF: Q4 vs Q1 HR 1.84\nAlbumin        ↓: Congestion, inflammation, malnutrition,  ↑: Dehydration only              In-hospital mortality 4× higher (OR 3.77)\n                   hemodilution, PLE, cachexia                                               AUC 0.73 comparable to BNP\nINR             Hepatic congestion, VitK deficiency, ACLI   Low = hypercoagulable (rare)    HR 1.89 per 0.1 increase (Okada 2016)\n\nKey Pearls: PVPI >0.5 = 81%/87% Sn/Sp for congestion-driven TBili elevation  |  ALT:LDH <1.5 = ischemic over viral  |  Two-hit required for ACLI\nSAGB ≥1.1 = cardiac/portal etiology of ascites  |  Infiltrative CM (amyloid, hemochromatosis) affects BOTH heart + liver — not congestive hepatopathy",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "angle": 0, "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "index": "aj3"
    },

